ities, medical office and life science properties and other healthcare related properties; industrial logistics properties trusts that owns and leases industrial and logistics properties; office properties income trust which owns and leases office properties primarily to single tenants and those with high credit quality characteristics; and service properties trust. It also provides advisory services to publicly traded mortgage real estate investment trust. In addition, the company provides management services to franchisor and operator of hotels, resorts and cruise ships; private funds, joint ventures and the underlying residential real estate assets of the funds, as well as property management services to third party owners; and private capital vehicles, including ABP trust and other private entities that own commercial real estate. The company was formerly known as REIT Management & Research Inc. and changed its name to The RMR Group Inc. in October 2015. The RMR Group Inc. was founded in 1986 and is headquartered in Newton, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Adam David Portnoy | CEO, President, MD & Chairman | Age 55 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["The RMR Group Inc. is a micro-cap real estate business with a $286M market cap on $643M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -13% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -4.9pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 39% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 30-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $65M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.77\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.5\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 11.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -4.9pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 16% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 67% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the 